# Comments Test

Tests single-line comments (`///`) and multi-line comments.
The rule (doc/altodo_spec.md, 3.2.3): the first line of a multi-line comment is indented by exactly the previous task / `///` line + 4 spaces. The same indentation continues the comment.


## Single-Line Comments

/// This is a standalone single-line comment
[ ] Task with a single-line comment below
    /// This is a note for the task above
[ ] + Task with a starred note
    /// + A single-line comment can have a flag
    /// !! Even a priority flag


## Nested Single-Line Comments

[ ] + Parent task -> 2099-10-10
    /// Comment for parent
    [ ] + Child task -> 2099-10-10
        /// Comment for child
        [ ] + Grandchild task -> 2099-10-10
            /// Comment for grandchild


## Multi-Line Comments (OK)

[ ] + Task with multi-line comment
    This is the first line of the comment.
    This is the second line.
    This is the third line.

[ ] Task with Markdown in the comment
    A **bold** word, an *italic* word and `inline code`.
    - list item 1
    - list item 2
    1. numbered item
    [A link](https://example.com) is a comment line, not a task.
    ```
    [ ] a task-like line in a fenced code block is comment text
    ```


## Multi-Line Comments with Empty Lines (OK)

The line below the second one has only spaces (4 of them), so the comment continues.

[ ] + Task with space-only lines in the comment
    First line of comment.
    Second line of comment.
    
    Fourth line (third line contains only spaces).
    Fifth line.


## Nested Multi-Line Comments (OK)

[ ] Parent task
    Parent task comment line 1.
    Parent task comment line 2.
    [ ] Child task
        Child task comment line 1.
        Child task comment line 2.
        
        Child task comment line 4.


## Description and Note (OK)

The description comes first (part of the task). The `///` note follows (detached note).

[ ] Task with a description and a note
    This is the description of the task.
    It is part of the task definition.
    /// This is a note, not part of the task.
        A multi-line comment under a note: the note's indentation + 4 spaces.


## Not Multi-Line Comments (NG)

The lines marked "NG" must look like normal Markdown text, not like comments.

[ ] Parent task
    [ ] Child task
    NG: same indentation as the child task (not child + 4 spaces).

[ ] Task with a comment that is too deep
            NG: task + 12 spaces (not task + 4 spaces).

[ ] Task with a comment after an empty line
    OK: the first comment line.

    NG: the line above is completely empty (zero characters), so the comment ended.

[ ] Task with a note
    /// A note
    NG: same indentation as the note (not note + 4 spaces).

[ ] Task whose comment has a deeper line
    OK: comment line.
        NG: deeper indentation (for example a nested list) is not part of the comment.

NG: this line has no indentation, so it is normal text.


## Comments with Special Characters (OK)

[ ] Task with special chars in comment
    Comment with symbols: !@#$%^&*()
    Comment with numbers: 1234567890
    Comment with punctuation: .,;:'"?!
